-- Metadata-only rename window on db8000: SCTN /-SR-CSV-S6137-BAR-3 (=24384/25639,
-- owner FRMW /-SR-CSV-S6137/MAIN). A SCTN is a model unit (e3d-model
-- is_model_unit), so with the metadata gate off this single NAME change rolls up
-- to the SCTN itself (regenerate = 1 unit) and with the gate on it rolls up to
-- nothing: exactly the shape the pinned live gate
-- (AIOS_METADATA_ONLY_WINDOW=base:target) asserts.
--
-- Why not the EQUI /1-LNR-Q005-PJ the first draft used: EQUI is a generation
-- root, not a model unit, so renaming it is no_model with the gate off as well
-- and the pinned gate would report saved_units=0 and go red.
--
-- Only NAME is written, exactly one SAVEWORK, no QUIT/FINISH (the l3_suite
-- driver wrapper owns the session). Navigation is by refno, which holds on this
-- channel (see db8000_bran_ftub_move_apply.mac).
-- restore partner: codex_md_rename_restore.mac
--
-- History: the 2026-09-08 15:0x drafts of this file crashed E3D TTY with
-- 0xC0000005 before their first log line. Lines 10 and 20 of those drafts
-- carried a literal editor line-number prefix (four spaces, the number, a
-- vertical bar) pasted from a read-out, which PML cannot parse. Keep this
-- file free of such prefixes.

ALPHA LOG "D:/work/plant-code/old/gen-model/scripts/e3d/codex_md_rename_apply.log" OVER
$P CODEX-MD-RENAME-APPLY-ALIVE
Q PROJ
Q MDB
=24384/25639
Q CE
Q TYPE
Q NAME
Q OWNE
NAME /-SR-CSV-S6137-BAR-3_CODEXMD
Q CE
Q NAME
Q OWNE
SAVEWORK 'CODEX metadata only rename of SCTN -SR-CSV-S6137-BAR-3'
$P CODEX-MD-RENAME-APPLY-DONE
ALPHA LOG END
